# Everything this repository generates goes in build/, and build/ is ignored
# whole. One rule rather than a list that has to be kept in step with the
# scripts — a generated file that lands next to its source is how a working
# tree ends up dirty for reasons nobody can account for, and how a stray file
# ends up inside a packaged extension.
build/

# Signing material. A .p12 holds a private key — the one thing in this
# repository that could not be regenerated and must never be committed.
cert/

# Dependencies
node_modules/

# BENCO style guides, shared across apps rather than owned by this one
style/

# Screenshots of the UI, regenerated by tools/preview.sh whenever they are
# wanted. Kept out of build/ because they are looked at rather than built.
screenshots/

# The test browser profile, kept between runs so the test vault survives.
# Not build output: deleting it loses a vault, which build/ implies it would not.
.bencpass-profile/

# Anything the server has been asked to store while running locally
server/data/

# `go build` with no -o drops the binary beside its source, and it is not
# covered by build/ above. Twelve megabytes of it reached two commits before
# anyone noticed, carrying the absolute paths of the machine that compiled it.
# tools/build-server.sh writes to build/ and is the way to produce one.
server/server
server/*.exe

# Editors and operating systems, which scatter these through a working tree and
# have never once been worth committing.
.DS_Store
._*
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
*~
*.log

# Worktrees, which Claude Code creates here when an agent works in isolation.
# They are checkouts of this repository, so committing one would nest a copy of
# the tree inside itself.
.claude/
